cms7h5z3s000pqq0kx17w7qme	10-health-benefits-of-finger-millet-kodo-you-should-know	10 Health Benefits of Finger Millet (Kodo) You Should Know	{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":", commonly known as "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https://www.arkshfood.com/products?name=kodo","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-blue-500 hover:text-blue-700 underline cursor-pointer"}},{"type":"bold"},{"type":"italic"}],"text":"kodo"},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"},{"type":"italic"}],"text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in Nepal, has been part of traditional Nepali diets for generations. Long before people began searching for superfoods and healthier grains, families across Nepal were already using "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"kodo"},{"type":"text","text":" to prepare dhido, roti, porridge, and fermented foods."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Today, this traditional grain is finding its way back into modern kitchens through flour, cookies, biscuits, breakfast dishes, and convenient packaged snacks."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"The renewed interest is not surprising. "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" provides "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"dietary fibre"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"complex carbohydrates"},{"type":"text","text":", calcium, minerals, and naturally occurring plant compounds. According to the Food and Agriculture Organization, 100 grams of "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" provides approximately 336 calories, 6.7 grams of protein, 11.2 grams of "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"dietary fibre"},{"type":"text","text":", and 67.3 grams of available carbohydrates. It is also rich in nutrients such as magnesium, phosphorus, copper, selenium, and thiamine."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"However, "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"finger millet benefits"},{"type":"text","text":" depend on how the grain is processed, prepared, and included within the rest of your diet. It should be seen as a nutritious grain rather than a miracle food."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Here are ten reasons "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" deserves a place in a balanced everyday diet."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"What Is Finger Millet?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" is a small-seeded cereal grain scientifically known as Eleusine coracana. It is widely grown in parts of Africa and South Asia, including Nepal."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"In Nepali households, "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"kodo"},{"type":"text","text":" has traditionally been used to make:"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dhido"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Roti"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Porridge"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fermented foods and beverages"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Flour-based snacks"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Biscuits and cookies"},{"type":"hardBreak"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" can tolerate difficult growing conditions and generally requires fewer resources than many major cereal crops. Millets can grow in relatively poor soils and withstand challenging climatic conditions, making them valuable for both food security and "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"sustainable agriculture"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Its renewed popularity shows that "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https://www.arkshfood.com/blog/what-makes-millet-snacks-different-from-regular-wheat-based-biscuits","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-blue-500 hover:text-blue-700 underline cursor-pointer"}},{"type":"bold"},{"type":"italic"}],"text":"traditional grains"},{"type":"text","text":" can still fit naturally into modern eating habits."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"1. Finger Millet Is Naturally Rich in Calcium"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"One of the most widely discussed "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"benefits of finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" is its naturally high calcium content."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Research reviews have reported that "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" contains approximately 344 milligrams of calcium per 100 grams, although the exact amount can vary depending on variety, soil, processing, and preparation. It is often recognised as containing more calcium than most commonly consumed cereal grains."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Calcium is important for:"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Maintaining bones and teeth"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Supporting normal muscle function"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Helping nerves communicate"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Supporting several normal processes within the body"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"This makes "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" a useful grain to include in a varied diet alongside other calcium sources."},{"type":"hardBreak"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"However, eating "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"kodo"},{"type":"text","text":" alone does not guarantee strong bones. Vitamin D, physical activity, protein intake, age, and overall nutrition also matter."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"2. It Provides a Good Amount of Dietary Fibre"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" is naturally rich in "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"dietary fibre"},{"type":"text","text":", particularly when the grain is consumed in a less-refined or "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"whole-grain"},{"type":"text","text":" form."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"The FAO reports approximately 11.2 grams of "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"dietary fibre"},{"type":"text","text":" per 100 grams of "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":", while other reviews have found higher levels depending on the grain variety and analytical method used."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Fibre helps support:"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Normal digestion"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Regular bowel movements"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Greater fullness after eating"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A balanced gut environment"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"More gradual digestion of carbohydrate-containing meals"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"A high-fibre meal may help you feel satisfied for longer than one made mainly with heavily refined flour."},{"type":"hardBreak"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"That does not mean every "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" product is automatically high in fibre. Milling, removing the outer grain layers, and mixing millet with refined flour can change the final nutritional value."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Always check the ingredient list and nutrition label when buying packaged "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"kodo biscuits"},{"type":"text","text":", flour, or snacks."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"3. Finger Millet Can Help You Feel Fuller"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Foods containing fibre generally take longer to eat and digest than highly refined foods. Because "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" contains fibre and "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"complex carbohydrates"},{"type":"text","text":", it can contribute to a "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https://www.arkshfood.com/blog/the-psychology-of-snacking-why-we-crave-crunchy-foods-and-how-to-snack-smarter","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-blue-500 hover:text-blue-700 underline cursor-pointer"}},{"type":"bold"},{"type":"italic"}],"text":"more satisfying meal or snack."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https://www.arkshfood.com/blog/the-psychology-of-snacking-why-we-crave-crunchy-foods-and-how-to-snack-smarter","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-blue-500 hover:text-blue-700 underline cursor-pointer"}}]},{"type":"text","text":"This can be useful for people who often feel hungry shortly after eating refined snacks."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"For example, "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" may be included in:"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Breakfast porridge"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Roti served with vegetables or lentils"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Dhido with a balanced tarkari"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Biscuits paired with milk or fruit"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Homemade snacks combined with nuts or seeds"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"The rest of the meal still matters. A small "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"kodo"},{"type":"text","text":" biscuit and a complete "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" meal will not provide the same level of fullness or nutrition."},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"For better balance, combine the grain with vegetables, fruit, dairy, pulses, eggs, nuts, or another source of protein."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"4. It May Support More Balanced Blood Sugar Responses"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Many people associate millet with better "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"blood sugar"},{"type":"text","text":" management. There is some supporting research, but the subject requires careful explanation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"A systematic review and meta-analysis found that millets generally had a lower average "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"glycaemic index"},{"type":"text","text":" than refined wheat and milled rice. Some studies also reported improvements in fasting or post-meal blood glucose when millets were consumed regularly. However, the results varied by millet type, processing method, recipe, and study design."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"This means "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" may support a more gradual "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"blood sugar"},{"type":"text","text":" response when:"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"It is eaten in a less-refined form"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The portion is reasonable"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"It replaces a more refined grain"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"It is paired with fibre, protein, and healthy fats"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The overall meal is balanced"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Processing can make a major difference. Finely ground flour, added sugar, sweeteners, or highly processed recipes may affect blood glucose differently from whole or minimally processed millet."},{"type":"hardBreak"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"People with diabetes should not treat "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"kodo"},{"type":"text","text":" as a medication or assume every millet product is suitable for unlimited consumption. Individual needs vary, so professional dietary guidance remains important."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"5. Finger Millet Contains Naturally Occurring Antioxidant Compounds"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" contains plant compounds known as polyphenols, particularly in its outer layers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"These compounds have antioxidant activity, which means they can help protect cells from oxidative stress. Research reviews have identified phenolic acids, tannins, and other phytochemicals in "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Antioxidant-rich foods are valuable as part of a varied diet containing:"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fruits"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Vegetables"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pulses"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nuts and seeds"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Whole grains"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Herbs and spices"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" should not be presented as a treatment for disease simply because it contains antioxidants. Its real value comes from contributing useful nutrients and plant compounds to a balanced eating pattern."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"6. It Offers Useful Minerals and Micronutrients"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" provides more than fibre and calcium."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"The FAO identifies "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" as being high in nutrients such as:"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Magnesium"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Phosphorus"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Copper"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Selenium"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Thiamine"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"It is also a source of iron."},{"type":"hardBreak"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"These nutrients support different functions in the body. For example:"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Iron contributes to normal oxygen transport."},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Magnesium supports muscles, nerves, and energy metabolism."},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Phosphorus contributes to bones, teeth, and cellular processes."},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Copper supports iron metabolism and connective tissues."},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Thiamine helps the body release energy from food."},{"type":"hardBreak"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The amount absorbed by the body can be affected by preparation methods and naturally occurring compounds such as phytates and tannins."},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Soaking, fermenting, malting, and germinating millet may change digestibility and nutrient availability. The final benefit depends not only on what the raw grain contains but also on how it is prepared."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"7. It Is Naturally Gluten-Free"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" is naturally free from gluten."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"That makes it a useful grain for people who need to avoid gluten because of coeliac disease, non-coeliac gluten sensitivity, or another medically diagnosed condition."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"It can be used in:"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Gluten-free"},{"type":"text","text":" flour blends"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Porridge"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Flatbreads"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pancakes"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cookies"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Biscuits"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Baked snacks"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"However, a product made with "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" is not automatically "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"gluten-free"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Packaged foods may also contain:"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Wheat flour"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Barley"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Other gluten-containing grains"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Ingredients processed on shared equipment"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Anyone who must strictly avoid gluten should check the complete ingredient list and look for reliable "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"gluten-free"},{"type":"text","text":" labelling. Cross-contamination can still occur during farming, milling, manufacturing, or packaging."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"8. "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https://www.arkshfood.com/blog/what-makes-millet-snacks-different-from-regular-wheat-based-biscuits","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-blue-500 hover:text-blue-700 underline cursor-pointer"}},{"type":"bold"},{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Finger Millet Adds Variety to Everyday Grain Intake"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Many households depend heavily on rice and wheat. These grains can certainly be part of a balanced diet, but eating a wider range of grains can provide greater variety in nutrients, flavour, and texture."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Adding "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" allows families to rotate between:"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Rice"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Wheat"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Maize"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Oats"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Barley"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Buckwheat"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Finger millet"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Other local grains"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"This is one of the most practical "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"kodo benefits"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https://www.arkshfood.com/blog/why-more-nepali-families-are-choosing-healthy-biscuits","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer nofollow","class":"text-blue-500 hover:text-blue-700 underline cursor-pointer"}},{"type":"bold"},{"type":"italic"}],"text":"Healthy eating"},{"type":"text","text":" does not require completely replacing familiar foods. It can simply mean creating more variety across the week."},{"type":"hardBreak"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"A family might have rice at lunch, wheat roti at dinner, and "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" porridge or biscuits during breakfast or snack time. Small changes like this make "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"traditional grains"},{"type":"text","text":" easier to include without making the diet feel restrictive."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"9. It Connects Modern Nutrition With Traditional Nepali Food Culture"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" is not a newly invented wellness ingredient. It has deep roots in Nepal's food culture."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"For generations, Nepali communities have cultivated and consumed "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"kodo"},{"type":"text","text":" in everyday meals. Bringing it back into regular diets helps preserve:"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Traditional food knowledge"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Local recipes"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Familiar flavours"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Agricultural diversity"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Connections between farmers and consumers"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"This matters because modern convenience does not have to mean abandoning traditional ingredients."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Kodo"},{"type":"text","text":" can now be enjoyed through both traditional and modern foods, including dhido, roti, porridge, flour mixes, cookies, and "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"millet biscuits"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"When children encounter "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" through familiar snacks, they may become more comfortable with a grain that was already part of their grandparents' diets."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"10. Finger Millet Can Support More Sustainable Food Choices"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"benefits of finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" extend beyond personal nutrition."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Millets are generally recognised as climate-resilient crops. They can tolerate difficult conditions, grow in relatively poor soils, and contribute to food security in areas where other cereals may struggle."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Supporting millet-based foods may contribute to:"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Greater crop diversity"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"More resilient farming systems"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Demand for "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"traditional grains"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Opportunities for local farmers"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reduced dependence on only a few major cereals"},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"This does not mean every millet product is automatically sustainable. Farming methods, transportation, packaging, processing, and sourcing all matter."},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Still, choosing locally sourced millet products can help create more demand for crops already suited to regional farming conditions."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Finger Millet Nutrition: What Does Kodo Contain?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The nutritional profile varies by variety and processing method, but 100 grams of "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" contains approximately:"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"336 calories"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"67.3 grams of available carbohydrates"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"6.7 grams of protein"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"1.9 grams of fat"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"11.2 grams of "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"dietary fibre"},{"type":"hardBreak","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"Finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" is also high in thiamine, copper, magnesium, phosphorus, and selenium, while providing iron and other useful nutrients."},{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"These values apply to the grain itself. A biscuit, cookie, porridge, or flour blend will have a different nutritional profile depending on its full recipe, serving size, and preparation."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"textAlign":null,"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"How to Add Finger Millet to Your Diet"}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null}},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"You do not need to completely change your meals to enjoy the "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"benefits of finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"hardBreak"},{"type":"text","text":"Simple ways to include it are:"}]},{"type":"bulletList","content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Prepare "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"kodo"},{"type":"text","text":" dhido with vegetables and lentils."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Make "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"bold"}],"text":"finger millet"},{"type":"text","text":" roti."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cook millet porridge for breakfast."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","attrs":{"textAlign":null},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Mix millet flour with other flours."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":